`23 Sep 1974` MEANS `the calendar date` 23 9 1974
`1 Jan 1970` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 1 1970
`31 Aug 2023` MEANS `the calendar date` 31 8 2023
`29 Feb 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 29 2 2024
`1 Mar 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2024
`31 Aug 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 31 8 2025
`30 Dec 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 30 12 2025
`1 Jan 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 1 2026
`10 Jan 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 10 1 2026
`28 Feb 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 28 2 2026
`1 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2026
`1 Jun 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 6 2026
`2 Jun 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 2 6 2026
`30 Jun 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 30 6 2026
`1 Jul 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 7 2026
`10 Jul 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 10 7 2026
`11 Jul 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 11 7 2026
`1 Oct 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 10 2026
`7 Nov 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 7 11 2026
`1 Jun 2008` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 6 2008
`2 Jun 2008` MEANS `the calendar date` 2 6 2008
`29 Feb 2008` MEANS `the calendar date` 29 2 2008
`29 Feb 2012` MEANS `the calendar date` 29 2 2012
`28 Feb 2030` MEANS `the calendar date` 28 2 2030
`15 Mar 2015` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 3 2015
`15 Mar 2033` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 3 2033
`1 Oct 2044` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 10 2044

`COVERED` MEANS `yes: this Act applies to the death (s 5)`
`BEFORE 1974` MEANS `no: the death occurred before 23 September 1974; this Act applies only to later deaths, and the Compensation (Fatal Injuries) Ordinance 1938 as amended continues to apply (s 5(1), s 2(2), the text's no)`
`MOTOR ACCIDENT` MEANS `no: the death occurred in or as a result of a motor accident, and the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 precludes an action in respect of it (s 5(2), the text's no)`

`M SPOUSE` MEANS `yes: a spouse or de facto partner (s 4(2)(a))`
`M CHILD` MEANS `yes: a child, which includes an adopted child, a grandchild and a stepchild (s 4(1), s 4(2)(b))`
`M POSTHUMOUS` MEANS `yes: a child born alive after the death, treated as born before it (s 4(3)(b), s 4(2)(b))`
`M LOCO PARENTIS TO` MEANS `yes: a person to whom the deceased stood in loco parentis immediately before the death (s 4(2)(c); an infant is also treated as a child, s 4(3)(d))`
`M LOCO PARENTIS FROM` MEANS `yes: a person who stood in loco parentis to the deceased immediately before the death (s 4(2)(d))`
`M PARENT` MEANS `yes: a parent, which includes an adoptive parent, a step-parent and a grandparent (s 4(1), s 4(2)(e))`
`M SIBLING` MEANS `yes: a brother, sister, half-brother or half-sister (s 4(2)(f))`
`M FORMER` MEANS `yes: a former spouse or de facto partner (s 4(2)(g))`
`M NOT NAMED` MEANS `the Act does not name this relationship in s 4(2) or in its definitions of child and parent; it does not say whether you are a member of the family (NOTHING-kind)`
`other relationship` MEANS `some other relationship (for example aunt, uncle, cousin, niece, nephew, step-brother, step-sister, fiance or friend)`

`LIABLE` MEANS `yes: the person who would have been liable to the deceased is liable to an action for damages for the death, even if the death also amounts to an offence (s 7(1))`
`LIABLE DESPITE SETTLEMENT` MEANS `yes: the person who would have been liable to the deceased is liable to an action for damages for the death; the deceased's own settlement, release or judgment does not affect that liability, but a payment under it made within 6 months after the wrongful act is taken into account in the damages (s 7(2), s 10(5))`
`NOT LIABLE` MEANS `no, not under s 7: the death was not caused by a wrongful act, neglect or default for which the deceased could have sued had he or she lived (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
`S7 NOT UNDER THIS ACT` MEANS `not under this Act: it does not cover the death (s 5, the text's no)`

`I MAY BRING IT` MEANS `you may bring the action yourself, in your own name, for the benefit of every member of the family who sustained damage because of the death; the writ must name each of them and their relationship to the deceased (s 13, s 14)`
`NOT YET` MEANS `not yet: until 6 months after the death only the personal representative may bring the action, for your benefit and the benefit of the other members of the family who sustained damage (s 8(2), s 13(1))`
`ONE ACTION ONLY` MEANS `no new action: not more than one action may be brought against any one person in respect of a death (s 8(1), the text's no); the action already brought is for the benefit of every member of the family who sustained damage, and if your name was left out, see s 15`
`NO DAMAGE` MEANS `the action is not for your benefit: it is for the members of the family who sustained damage because of the death (s 8(2), the text's no)`
`NOT NAMED` MEANS `the Act does not name your relationship among the members of the family; it does not say whether the action is for your benefit (NOTHING-kind)`
`S8 NOT UNDER THIS ACT` MEANS `not under this Act: it does not cover the death, so no action lies under it (s 5, the text's no)`

`H LOSS` MEANS `damages the court thinks proportioned to the injury resulting from the death, such as lost financial support (s 10(1))`
`H BURIAL` MEANS `the reasonable expenses of burial or disposal of the remains (s 10(3)(a))`
`H MEDICAL` MEANS `the reasonable medical and hospital expenses of the deceased for the fatal injury (s 10(3)(b))`
`H CONSORTIUM` MEANS `damages for loss or impairment of consortium, for the surviving spouse or de facto partner (s 10(3)(c))`
`H HOUSEHOLD` MEANS `the reasonable expenses of hiring help to perform the household services the deceased customarily performed (s 10(3)(d))`
`H CARER` MEANS `the reasonable expenses of hiring a person to live in the home and care for the infant child until 18 (s 10(3)(e)(i))`
`H GUIDANCE` MEANS `damages for the infant child's loss of the deceased's care and guidance as a parent (s 10(3)(e)(ii))`
`H SOLATIUM` MEANS `solatium: money for grief and suffering (s 10(3)(f))`

`NOT AN INFANT` MEANS `not under s 10(3)(e): the child was not an infant when the deceased died (the text's no: its "if" fails)`

`NO REDUCTION` MEANS `no: no reduction may be made on account of it in assessing the damages (s 10(4), the text's no)`
`TAKEN INTO ACCOUNT` MEANS `yes: it must be taken into account in assessing the damages, since the deceased's settlement, release or judgment was made within 6 months after the wrongful act (s 10(5))`
`ACT SILENT ON LATE SETTLEMENT` MEANS `the Act does not say: s 10(5) reaches only a settlement, release or judgment made within 6 months after the wrongful act, and this one was made later (NOTHING-kind)`
`the deceased's settlement` MEANS `a payment under a settlement, release or judgment the deceased made, gave or obtained for the wrongful act before dying`

`PAID OUT` MEANS `yes: the court has ordered it, and money paid into court is paid out under the court's order (s 12(2))`
`ONLY BY ORDER` MEANS `not without an order of the court: no part of the money paid into court may be paid out except under an order of the court (s 12(2), the text's no)`
`NOTHING PAID IN` MEANS `s 12 does not arise: the defendant has not paid money into court (the text's no: its "where" fails)`

`NAMED` MEANS `your name is in the action: it is brought for your benefit (s 14); the court may also order that you be separately represented (s 15(2))`
`COURT MAY ADD ME` MEANS `the court may order the action to proceed as if your name had been included, on your application or of its own motion (s 15(1)); whether it does is the court's discretion; it may also order separate representation (s 15(2))`
`COURT NOT SATISFIED` MEANS `s 15(1) does not arise: the court is not satisfied that your name should have been included (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
`NO ACTION YET` MEANS `s 15 does not arise: no action has been commenced (the text's no: its "where" fails); see s 8 and s 13 on who may bring one`

§ `The dates`

-- 10 January to 10 July 2026: 21 + 28 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 30 + 10 = 181 days.
#ASSERT `the last day of 6 months after` `10 Jan 2026` EQUALS `10 Jul 2026`
#ASSERT `the days from` `10 Jan 2026` `to` `10 Jul 2026` EQUALS 181
-- 31 August plus 6 months: the last day of February (common year, then leap year).
#ASSERT `the last day of 6 months after` `31 Aug 2025` EQUALS `28 Feb 2026`
#ASSERT `the last day of 6 months after` `31 Aug 2023` EQUALS `29 Feb 2024`
-- Across a year end.
#ASSERT `the last day of 6 months after` `30 Dec 2025` EQUALS `30 Jun 2026`
-- 18th birthdays, including one from 29 February (28 February in a common year).
#ASSERT `the day of the 18th birthday of` `15 Mar 2015` EQUALS `15 Mar 2033`
#ASSERT `the day of the 18th birthday of` `29 Feb 2012` EQUALS `28 Feb 2030`
#ASSERT `the day of the 18th birthday of` `29 Feb 2008` EQUALS `28 Feb 2026`

§ `s 5 -- does this Act cover the death`

-- Death on the commencement day (edge).
#ASSERT `s 5 -- does this Act cover the death` `23 Sep 1974` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `COVERED`
-- Death the day before (edge): the 1938 Ordinance (s 2(2)).
#ASSERT `s 5 -- does this Act cover the death` `22 Sep 1974` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `BEFORE 1974`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- does this Act cover the death` `1 Jan 1970` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `BEFORE 1974`
-- A recent death, not a motor accident; the "not precluded" answer is ignored.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- does this Act cover the death` `10 Jan 2026` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `COVERED`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- does this Act cover the death` `10 Jan 2026` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `COVERED`
-- A motor accident death where the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act precludes an action.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- does this Act cover the death` `10 Jan 2026` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `MOTOR ACCIDENT`
-- A motor accident death where that Act leaves an action open.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- does this Act cover the death` `10 Jan 2026` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `COVERED`
-- The date is checked first.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- does this Act cover the death` `1 Jan 1970` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `BEFORE 1974`

§ `s 4 -- am I a member of the family`

#ASSERT `s 4 -- am I a member of the family` `spouse` EQUALS `M SPOUSE`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- am I a member of the family` `de facto partner` EQUALS `M SPOUSE`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- am I a member of the family` `former spouse` EQUALS `M FORMER`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- am I a member of the family` `former de facto partner` EQUALS `M FORMER`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- am I a member of the family` `child, including an adopted child` EQUALS `M CHILD`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- am I a member of the family` `grandchild` EQUALS `M CHILD`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- am I a member of the family` `stepchild` EQUALS `M CHILD`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- am I a member of the family` `child born alive after the death` EQUALS `M POSTHUMOUS`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- am I a member of the family` `a person to whom the deceased stood in loco parentis immediately before the death` EQUALS `M LOCO PARENTIS TO`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- am I a member of the family` `a person who stood in loco parentis to the deceased immediately before the death` EQUALS `M LOCO PARENTIS FROM`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- am I a member of the family` `parent, including an adoptive parent` EQUALS `M PARENT`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- am I a member of the family` `step-father or step-mother` EQUALS `M PARENT`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- am I a member of the family` `grandfather or grandmother` EQUALS `M PARENT`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- am I a member of the family` `brother or sister` EQUALS `M SIBLING`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- am I a member of the family` `half-brother or half-sister` EQUALS `M SIBLING`
-- An aunt, a cousin, a step-brother: not named; the list is not closed with "only" (NOTHING-kind, fork F2).
#ASSERT `s 4 -- am I a member of the family` `other relationship` EQUALS `M NOT NAMED`
#ASSERT `I am named as a member of the family` `former spouse`
#ASSERT NOT (`I am named as a member of the family` `other relationship`)

§ `s 7 -- is the wrongdoer liable`

-- Negligence that would have let the deceased sue; no settlement.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- is the wrongdoer liable` `10 Jan 2026` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `LIABLE`
-- The deceased settled before dying: liability unaffected (s 7(2)), subject to s 10(5).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- is the wrongdoer liable` `10 Jan 2026` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `LIABLE DESPITE SETTLEMENT`
-- Not caused by a wrongful act.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- is the wrongdoer liable` `10 Jan 2026` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NOT LIABLE`
-- Wrongful, but the deceased could not have sued (for example a complete defence).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- is the wrongdoer liable` `10 Jan 2026` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NOT LIABLE`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- is the wrongdoer liable` `10 Jan 2026` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `NOT LIABLE`
-- A motor accident death that the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act takes out: s 5 first.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- is the wrongdoer liable` `10 Jan 2026` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `S7 NOT UNDER THIS ACT`
-- A motor accident death where an action is still open.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- is the wrongdoer liable` `10 Jan 2026` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `LIABLE`
-- A death before commencement.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- is the wrongdoer liable` `22 Sep 1974` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `S7 NOT UNDER THIS ACT`

